### Task 4 — Validity Audit

| Threat to Validity | Description | Control / Disclosure |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Hardware Heterogeneity** | Differences in memory bandwidth between CPU (DDR) and GPU (VRAM) skew results. | Disclosure of exact memory bandwidth (GB/s) for each backend. |
| **Software/Driver Overhead** | Vulkan and CUDA have different driver/runtime initialization costs. | Use a "warm-up" run for each backend before recording measurements. |
| **Concurrency/Threading** | The CPU is limited to 8 threads, while GPU backends use massive parallelism. | Use a fixed thread count for CPU and specify the GPU kernel concurrency/grid size. |
| **Workload Comparability** | Different backends might use different math kernels (e.g., different rounding/precision) for the same model. | **Control:** Verify that the output logits or text generation for all three backends are identical (or within a specific epsilon) for the same seed. |

